  "report_period": "Week 46 (7th Nov to 14th Nov 2025)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "Seacon Shipping Group have committed the Newcastlemax \"Seacon Africa\" 206/2006 Imabari, Japan (SS/DD 06/2026) to clients of Tianjin Global Shipping at USD 22,7 mill. For reference, the sister vessel \"Samc MG\" 206/2006 Imabari, Japan (SS/DD 10/2026) was committed in October at USD 25 mill. The Ultramax \"Hako\" 63/2014 Yangzhou, China (SS 06/2029, DD 05/2027) of GSD Holding was committed at USD 22 mill. Remind you that the one- year-younger \"Beauty Lily\" 63/2015 CSI, China (SS 01/2030, DD 01/2028) was sold a month ago at USD 22,25 mill. In addition, the \"Grace Harmony\" 60/2015 Onomichi, Japan (SS 07/2030, DD 05/2028) from Ocean-Front Shipping was committed at high USD 24 mill, while the one-year-younger \"Imabari Queen\" 60/2016 Sanoyas, Japan (SS/DD 05/2026, Scrubber fitted) was sold a month ago at USD 23,5 mill. On the Supramax sector, AB Maritime committed their \"Aggeliki B\" 56/2011 Jiangsu, China (SS/DD 05/2026) at USD 13,4 mill. Note that the one-year- younger sister vessel \"Jin Mao\" 56/2012 Jiangsu, China (SS/DD 05/2027) was sold a month ago at USD 13,2 mill. Oskar Wehr have committed their Handysize \"Emil Selmer\" 32/2010 Jiangsu, China (SS/DD 12/2025) at USD 8 mill. For comparison, the one-year- older \"Golden Maple\" 32/2009 Zhejiang, China (SS 06/2029, DD 06/2027) was committed a week ago at USD 7,4 mill.",
    "tankers": "Scorpio Tankers have committed their four MR's \"STI Battery\" 50/2014 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS 11/2029, DD 12/2027, Scrubber fitted), \"STI Milwaukee\" 50/2014 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS 11/2029, DD 11/2027, Scrubber fitted), \"STI Venere\" 50/2014 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS 06/2029, DD 12/2027, Scrubber fitted) & \"STI Yorkville\" 50/2014 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS 10/2029, DD 10/2027, Scrubber fitted) to clients of TORM at USD 32 mill each. Note that a week ago, the one-year-younger \"Hellas Avatar\" 50/2015 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS 09/2030, DD 09/2028) was committed at USD 31,83 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "Iron ore rates on the West Australia / China route continued throughout",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 17,000/19,000 pd. A number of Indonesian and Australian trips into China were reported fixed in the usd 17,000/20,000 pd range. Indonesian and Australian trips into India were reported at the level of usd 17,000/19,000 pd. South East Asian trips via South America into China were fixed around usd 18,000/19,000 pd. Indian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 16,000/19,000 pd. West African trips into Continent were fixed around usd 11,000/12,000 pd. Inter- Continental trips via Red Sea were reported at the level of usd 14,000/15,000 pd. Continental trips via US East Coast into India were fixed around usd 25,000/27,000 pd. US Gulf trips into China were reported at the level of usd 22,000/24,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 800K/900K. South American trips into Continent were fixed around usd 28,000/29,000 pd. On the period front, Kamsarmaxes were reported fixed in the usd 16,000/18,000 pd for short period and usd 16,000/17,000 pd for long period employment basis delivery China.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "A number of Indonesian trips into China were reported fixed in the usd 13,000/16,000 pd range. Indian trips into China were fixed around usd 9,000/11,000 pd. Arabian Gulf trips into East Coast India were reported at the level of usd 19,000/20,000 pd. South African trips into China were fixed around usd 17,000/20,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 170K/200K. West African trips into China were reported at the level of usd 13,000/15,000 pd. Continental trips into Mediterranean were fixed around usd 20,000/23,000 pd. Inter-Mediterranean trips via East Coast South America were reported at the level of usd 13,000/14,000 pd. Mediterranean trips via West Coast India into East Coast India were fixed around usd 17,000/18,000 pd. US Gulf trips into Continent were reported at the level of usd 26,000/28,000 pd. South American trips into India were fixed around usd 17,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 700K. On the period front, an Ultramax was reported fixed in the usd 17,000 pd for 5/7 months employment basis delivery China.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "A number of Indonesian trips into China were reported fixed in the usd 8,000/11,000 pd range. South East Asian trips into US Gulf were reported at the level of usd 11,000/12,000 pd. West African trips into US Gulf were fixed around usd 9,000/10,000 pd. West African trips via Baltic into West Coast Central America were reported at the level of usd 14,000/16,000 pd. Continental trips via Mediterranean into West Africa were fixed around usd 16,000/17,000 pd. US Gulf coastal trips were reported at the level of usd 20,000/22,000 pd. US Gulf trips into Continent were fixed around usd 19,000/21,000 pd. South American coastal trips were reported at the level of usd 16,000/18,000 pd. South American trips into Continent were fixed around usd 15,000/17,000 pd. No period activity to report here."
    }
  },
